Fabulous.

280
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:20,440
Maybe go for something else...

281
00:12:20,730 --> 00:12:21,680
That'd be great, yeah?

282
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,600
So, where are you flying to this time?

283
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:25,490
I'm flying to Korea.

284
00:12:25,510 --> 00:12:26,500
Though...

285
00:12:26,690 --> 00:12:28,320
Paris is right around the corner.

286
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,660
Mm...

287
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:30,960
Oh, and...

288
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,320
Who do we have here?

289
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:34,040
Enjoying the conversation, huh?

290
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:35,970
Hello.

291
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:37,640
Hi.

292
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,070
Come on. I'm gonna take him to see Wut.

293
00:12:40,090 --> 00:12:40,690
Mm-hm.

294
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:42,690
Good luck, boy.

295
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:44,690
One day,

296
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:46,090
you'll be as famous...

297
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:47,120
as me!

298
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:52,160
So famous that you wanna retire!

299
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:53,020
Woo!

300
00:12:56,030 --> 00:12:57,120
Let's go. Come on.

301
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:58,960
See ya.

302
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,600
Compared to the series...

303
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,520
he seems different in real life, huh?

304
00:13:07,810 --> 00:13:08,440
Mm,

305
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:09,930
because this is real life.

306
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:10,860
What you just witnessed...

307
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:12,160
was a real person.

308
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,700
It gets even more real from here.

309
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:15,890
You'll get it after some time.

310
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:16,520
Come on,

311
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:18,140
let's go see Wut.

312
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,370
- Hello.
- Come take a seat.

313
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:30,980
Hi.

314
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:31,930
Take a seat.

315
00:13:36,170 --> 00:13:37,630
Tell me your personal background

316
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:39,200
in detail.

317
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:40,690
Right.

318
00:13:40,970 --> 00:13:41,780
I'm...

319
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:44,240
Wan, Ashawin Kosonkasem,

320
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:45,900
21 years old.

321
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,410
I'm a senior in my second semester,

322
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:49,520
majoring in Public Relations
in the Communication Arts program.

323
00:13:50,010 --> 00:13:51,470
I have one sister.

324
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:52,960
I'm from Ayutthaya.

325
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:54,760
My parents run a boat noodle shop.

326
00:13:54,850 --> 00:13:57,240
In high school,
I came to study in Bangkok.

327
00:13:57,770 --> 00:13:59,440
I'm living in my relative's condo

328
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:01,330
with my little sister.

329
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,360
Okay.

330
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:06,620
From now on,
our schedule will be absolutely packed,

331
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,280
starting today.

332
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:10,260
You're changing your look,

333
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:11,120
doing a fitting,

334
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,440
and filming the series.

335
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,160
Before the series, we're filming the pilot

336
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:16,000
and attending events.

337
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:17,880
As for the filming,

338
00:14:18,050 --> 00:14:19,670
it comes to around 50 cues per series,

339
00:14:19,690 --> 00:14:21,760
so you have to manage your time properly.

340
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,830
And if work starts flooding in,

341
00:14:24,150 --> 00:14:26,040
I'd suggest you drop the semester,

342
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,690
even though this is your last one.

343
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:30,680
Trust me. It's gonna be worth it.

344
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:33,470
Alright.

345
00:14:33,490 --> 00:14:35,170
So do you have any talent

346
00:14:35,190 --> 00:14:36,960
or something you're an expert at?

347
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:39,180
I can play the guitar.

348
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:41,920
I can also sing a little.

349
00:14:42,210 --> 00:14:43,000
However...

350
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,720
I don't know how to dance at all.

351
00:14:45,530 --> 00:14:47,240
For whatever skills you already have,

352
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,000
take more classes to improve them.

353
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:51,640
As for those you don't have,
you'll need to work on them,

354
00:14:51,790 --> 00:14:52,800
like dancing.

355
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:54,660
Sometimes, you need to attend events

356
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:56,300
or, like, fan-meeting stages.

357
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,940
You have to crush the performance

358
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,120
so as not to embarrass yourself.

359
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:00,610
Look at NuNew, for example.

360
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:01,190
That...

361
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:03,720
is the ideal bottom you have to become.

362
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:05,220
Alright.

363
00:15:06,970 --> 00:15:07,450
Come on now.

364
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:08,980
Sign the contract.

365
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:11,970
Uh...

366
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:13,800
I do have a question.

367
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:14,690
Hm?

368
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:18,690
So...

369
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,560
If I sign,

370
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:25,780
could I work part-time jobs
or take on extra gigs?

371
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:26,470
No,

372
00:15:27,610 --> 00:15:28,560
I don't think that's appropriate.

373
00:15:30,690 --> 00:15:31,220
Then...

374
00:15:31,490 --> 00:15:33,010
I'd rather not sign

375
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:37,940
because...

376
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,090
I'm not planning to become a celebrity.

377
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:42,210
I just want to earn money.

378
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:54,920
What's going on in your life?

379
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,760
My mom fell for a call-center scam,

380
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,860
so my family is in debt.

381
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:05,930
I have to help them make money.

382
00:16:06,690 --> 00:16:07,480
And...

383
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:10,500
those jobs I take on
are my main income.

384
00:16:11,590 --> 00:16:13,520
If you won't allow it,
I won't sign the contract.

385
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:24,210
How much do you owe?

386
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,290
500,000 baht.

387
00:16:36,490 --> 00:16:37,160
Fine!

388
00:16:44,690 --> 00:16:47,590
But I'm not letting you take on
photography gigs like before.

389
00:16:48,170 --> 00:16:50,000
I'll cover that 500,000 debt of yours.

390
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:52,320
On one condition:

391
00:16:52,770 --> 00:16:54,360
whatever you earn from now on,

392
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:56,520
half of your 70% share will be deducted

393
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:58,160
to pay the company back.

394
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,560
As for the rest, it's yours to keep.

395
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,480
This goes until you pay off the 500,000.

396
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:05,960
After that,
it's the normal 70:30 ratio.

397
00:17:06,599 --> 00:17:08,480
But if you breach the contract,

398
00:17:08,970 --> 00:17:12,099
you will be fined
2 million baht by the company.

399
00:17:12,550 --> 00:17:13,280
Do we have a deal?

400
00:17:14,550 --> 00:17:15,670
Yes, we have a deal.

401
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:16,490
Uh...

402
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,400
Then...

403
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,000
Please go ahead and transfer it.

404
00:17:22,569 --> 00:17:23,200
I'll...

405
00:17:23,450 --> 00:17:24,430
sign it right away.

406
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:26,700
Look at all that energy

407
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,880
compared to all that pondering earlier.

408
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:31,120
Sorry, sweetie.

409
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,920
I'll go ahead and modify the contract.

410
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:34,940
Make sure you write clear clauses.

411
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,860
Of course, gotta scan my face.

412
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:45,080
Well, you didn't remind me to get Botox.

413
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:46,080
My old face was like...

414
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:52,210
Mm.

415
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:53,270
It went through.

416
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,480
[Ashawin Kosonkasem]
[Artist]

417
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,360
Okay.

418
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:02,680
Welcome to...

419
00:18:02,850 --> 00:18:03,970
'Our House.'

420
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:06,630
Alright.

421
00:18:08,490 --> 00:18:09,400
Cue slogan.

422
00:18:10,290 --> 00:18:12,960
"Where every dream comes true!"

423
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:27,220
Renji.

424
00:18:28,070 --> 00:18:28,640
Oh?

425
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:30,640
This is Wan, our new boy.

426
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,380
Hello, Wan.

427
00:18:32,790 --> 00:18:33,560
I'm Ren.

428
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:34,800
Hm?

429
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,980
Oh, not just Ren.

430
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:38,800
I'm Renji.

431
00:18:40,210 --> 00:18:42,080
I'm not so used to the new name.

432
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:43,900
Uh...

433
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,040
Well...

434
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:46,830
Do I also have to change my name?

435
00:18:46,850 --> 00:18:47,640
Do you want to?

436
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:48,760
Wanwoon.

437
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:49,880
Wankim.

438
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:51,520
Two-syllable names are so on trend.

439
00:18:52,310 --> 00:18:52,970
Uh...

440
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,340
I think...

441
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:56,160
I'll sit this one out.

442
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:58,220
Okay.

443
00:18:58,450 --> 00:19:00,940
From now on, I will take care of you two.

444
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:02,530
Tell me if you need anything.

445
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:03,520
Don't hesitate.

446
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:04,680
Roger that.

447
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:07,230
Wan?

448
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:16,930
Though...

449
00:19:18,670 --> 00:19:19,920
we still need

450
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,760
to be considerate, right?

451
00:19:22,370 --> 00:19:23,180
Because I...

452
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:24,740
am only human.

453
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:26,600
Absolutely...

454
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:30,120
Both of you, listen to me.

455
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,860
In this industry,

456
00:19:32,310 --> 00:19:32,980
if you don't kill it,

457
00:19:33,530 --> 00:19:34,360
you're dead.

458
00:19:34,690 --> 00:19:35,440
If you don't get fierce,

459
00:19:35,650 --> 00:19:36,440
you flop.

460
00:19:36,810 --> 00:19:38,170
Therefore, both of you

461
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:40,520
will take an etiquette and poise course

462
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:42,080
and speech classes.

463
00:19:42,390 --> 00:19:44,690
More importantly,
you're visiting a beauty clinic

464
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:46,450
because your faces make you money.

465
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,240
I'll get you some consultations, sweeties.

466
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,540
But I already have my go-to clinic.

467
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:51,640
Don't worry about it.

468
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:52,720
Okay,

469
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:56,240
Wan, any questions?

470
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,970
So, like...

471
00:19:59,510 --> 00:20:01,240
Who will take care of the cost?

472
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:04,120
The company will.

473
00:20:04,850 --> 00:20:06,690
Then, I'm willing to do anything!

474
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,100
Okay.

475
00:20:08,490 --> 00:20:09,280
Lastly,

476
00:20:09,620 --> 00:20:11,700
listen carefully and take it to heart.

477
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:14,440
So long as you're not in a private room,

478
00:20:14,580 --> 00:20:16,330
no matter the situation,

479
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:18,070
do not frown,

480
00:20:18,090 --> 00:20:18,950
make faces,

481
00:20:18,970 --> 00:20:20,220
or look sullen.

482
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,360
You have to smile.

483
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,200
Are you done?

484
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,030
Uh, I have to go golfing with my friends.

485
00:20:35,370 --> 00:20:36,240
Excuse me.

486
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:37,390
Bye.

487
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:38,150
See ya.

488
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:39,120
Uh, hey...

489
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:39,520
Oh.

490
00:20:41,850 --> 00:20:43,010
It's gotta be a yes now, huh?

491
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:46,240
Then, I'll...

492
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:47,130
Hey, wait!

493
00:20:50,670 --> 00:20:52,670
Didn't Wut tell you
what you've gotta do?

494
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:54,680
You have to start at this second.

495
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,200
Come on, it's makeover time!

496
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:57,640
But Renji...

497
00:20:57,700 --> 00:21:00,070
He's already got one
since before the audition.

498
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:02,080
It's just... you now

499
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:05,500
who needs immediate help.

500
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:06,580
Let's go.

501
00:21:08,410 --> 00:21:09,600
Go, go, go.

502
00:21:09,620 --> 00:21:10,540
Walk up those stairs.

503
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:16,650
Everyone,

504
00:21:17,090 --> 00:21:18,000
he's here.

505
00:21:28,650 --> 00:21:30,080
Is this really a good idea, Cher?

506
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,600
Let's see.

507
00:21:38,730 --> 00:21:39,600
Your hair...

508
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,080
[Wan]

509
00:22:10,930 --> 00:22:11,920
Let me just say,

510
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:13,600
my makeup changed the game.

511
00:22:16,890 --> 00:22:18,490
The makeup serves the face.

512
00:22:18,510 --> 00:22:20,250
No, the hair does.

513
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:22,520
And my outfit serves that hair!

514
00:22:22,540 --> 00:22:23,760
How about we break this team up?

515
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:24,760
Just kidding, bestie.

516
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:25,560
It was a joke, yeah?

517
00:22:27,050 --> 00:22:28,040
Cher,

518
00:22:28,330 --> 00:22:29,420
this boy

519
00:22:29,750 --> 00:22:31,200
looks like he's gonna blow up.

520
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:32,310
Don't forget us then.

521
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:33,880
My boy here is ready to crash 'em.

522
00:22:37,620 --> 00:22:39,000
Right, okay.

523
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,080
We're all done, sweetie.

524
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:43,140
Come on, we still have
to sign you up for the classes.

525
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:48,760
[CREWAVE]

526
00:22:54,570 --> 00:22:55,760
All done.

527
00:22:56,260 --> 00:22:57,500
I'll get it taken care of nicely.

528
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:58,880
Thank you very much.

529
00:22:59,710 --> 00:23:00,440
Cher,

530
00:23:01,310 --> 00:23:02,960
I have to be in all these classes?

531
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:04,280
That's right.

532
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:05,920
Singing, acting, dancing,
you've gotta ace them all,

533
00:23:06,090 --> 00:23:07,400
just in case...

534
00:23:07,610 --> 00:23:09,280
you'll have your own single in the future.

535
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:11,720
Releasing a single, too?

536
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:12,240
Mm.

537
00:23:13,610 --> 00:23:15,480
I can't even get past acting yet.

538
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,360
Come on, just take the classes
now that you have the chance.

539
00:23:19,580 --> 00:23:20,640
Hello, Cher.

540
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:22,600
Hello, Tawan.

541
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:23,470
Oh.

542
00:23:23,490 --> 00:23:24,460
Hi, Third.

543
00:23:25,110 --> 00:23:26,490
I'll get the room ready.

544
00:23:37,590 --> 00:23:38,510
Congrats

545
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:40,840
on making the cut with a fluke.

546
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:52,120
Can't you really just walk past?

547
00:23:52,650 --> 00:23:53,700
No...

548
00:23:54,330 --> 00:23:55,120
Third,

549
00:23:55,440 --> 00:23:56,160
your bag.

550
00:23:56,460 --> 00:23:56,980
Alright.

551
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,000
Call me when you're done.

552
00:24:00,810 --> 00:24:01,570
Wan,

553
00:24:01,590 --> 00:24:02,310
let's go.

554
00:24:10,370 --> 00:24:11,400
I'm sorry.

555
00:24:23,330 --> 00:24:26,000
You're Wan, the boy who made the cut
for 'The Deep Between Us'

556
00:24:28,930 --> 00:24:29,800
Yes…

557
00:24:30,700 --> 00:24:32,480
Congratulations.

558
00:24:33,950 --> 00:24:34,990
Thank you...

559
00:24:35,010 --> 00:24:35,730
Lady.

560
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:40,000
Come on, Wan.

561
00:24:40,380 --> 00:24:42,210
Go home and rest. I'm taking you
to the clinic tomorrow

562
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:43,980
because I've got you an appointment.

563
00:24:46,490 --> 00:24:47,490
That boy...

564
00:24:48,010 --> 00:24:49,200
looks familiar

565
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,560
and sounds familiar,

566
00:24:51,870 --> 00:24:52,600
doesn't he?

567
00:24:52,920 --> 00:24:53,920
Not just familiar,

568
00:24:54,010 --> 00:24:54,880
that's the exact guy.

569
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:56,290
Whoa...

570
00:24:56,790 --> 00:24:57,790
That's not right.

571
