00:38:18,730 --> 00:38:20,320
you need to concentrate.

859
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:22,660
That's crucial.

860
00:38:23,070 --> 00:38:24,240
- Ah...
- Okay?

861
00:38:24,920 --> 00:38:26,100
Oh, okay.

862
00:38:26,730 --> 00:38:28,200
Right, if so,

863
00:38:28,590 --> 00:38:30,400
act for me.

864
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:32,900
I want to see how you guys look,

865
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:34,380
along with the script.

866
00:38:35,590 --> 00:38:37,400
Wan, Renji, act for me.

867
00:38:38,970 --> 00:38:40,520
Be active, be active.

868
00:38:44,260 --> 00:38:45,470
Uh...

869
00:38:46,040 --> 00:38:46,750
Luang,

870
00:38:46,770 --> 00:38:48,340
I don't have the lines memorized.

871
00:38:51,080 --> 00:38:52,280
Take the script with you, then.

872
00:38:53,020 --> 00:38:53,920
Thank you.

873
00:38:56,490 --> 00:38:58,780
Actually, I barely have any idea about it,

874
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:00,470
so let's do it
how we understand it, yeah?

875
00:39:02,290 --> 00:39:05,120
If you're done concentrating

876
00:39:05,140 --> 00:39:06,240
and ready,

877
00:39:06,520 --> 00:39:07,880
raise your hands.

878
00:39:17,610 --> 00:39:18,360
Three,

879
00:39:18,380 --> 00:39:19,000
two,

880
00:39:19,020 --> 00:39:19,720
one,

881
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:20,960
action.

882
00:39:24,330 --> 00:39:25,320
"Whoa, Heart.

883
00:39:25,850 --> 00:39:27,610
Long time no see. How have you been?"

884
00:39:34,400 --> 00:39:35,870
Hey, do you know how to high-five?

885
00:39:36,600 --> 00:39:37,600
Jeez, of course!

886
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,200
Uh, Pai.

887
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:41,140
May I try again?

888
00:39:41,160 --> 00:39:42,880
That's not a question, I'd say.

889
00:39:45,120 --> 00:39:46,350
Start over.

890
00:39:46,370 --> 00:39:47,610
But concentrate first.

891
00:39:47,710 --> 00:39:48,600
Take a deep breath.

892
00:39:51,160 --> 00:39:52,060
If you're ready...

893
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:55,360
And action.

894
00:39:56,340 --> 00:39:57,260
"Whoa, Heart.

895
00:39:57,280 --> 00:39:58,970
Long time no see. How have you been?"

896
00:40:01,610 --> 00:40:02,660
"It's been good.

897
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:05,760
Ever since I left the club,

898
00:40:05,780 --> 00:40:07,800
I've never seen anyone."

899
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:11,920
"But why the sad face?"

900
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:14,020
Uh...

901
00:40:14,430 --> 00:40:15,920
"Everyone's just the same.

902
00:40:16,300 --> 00:40:17,840
I also left the club."

903
00:40:18,540 --> 00:40:20,160
"You left the club?"

904
00:40:20,180 --> 00:40:21,030
"Mm."

905
00:40:21,250 --> 00:40:22,800
"What a shame."

906
00:40:27,050 --> 00:40:28,380
Uh...

907
00:40:28,660 --> 00:40:30,920
The script says "high-pitched voice."
Do I have to speak in a high pitch?

908
00:40:30,940 --> 00:40:32,560
Jeez, just keep it going.

909
00:40:32,580 --> 00:40:34,100
Follow the impulse.

910
00:40:34,120 --> 00:40:35,320
What is "impulse"?

911
00:40:42,220 --> 00:40:43,160
Translate it.

912
00:40:43,610 --> 00:40:44,560
Um...

913
00:40:44,750 --> 00:40:45,420
Well...

914
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:47,340
"The urges," yeah.

915
00:40:48,530 --> 00:40:49,890
Listen to the urges.

916
00:40:50,300 --> 00:40:51,200
Ah...

917
00:40:51,220 --> 00:40:52,030
Okay.

918
00:40:55,710 --> 00:40:57,660
So do I have to speak in a high pitch?

919
00:41:12,660 --> 00:41:14,960
Is that really important right now, Wan?

920
00:41:19,500 --> 00:41:20,650
Acting

921
00:41:21,240 --> 00:41:23,200
is not about putting on faces

922
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:25,000
and relying on the emotions on set.

923
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:30,720
Do you know
why I asked you that question,

924
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:32,480
especially you,

925
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:35,520
if you've read the script or the novel?

926
00:41:38,980 --> 00:41:42,080
It's about understanding
the role you're playing,

927
00:41:42,820 --> 00:41:44,800
what attitude they have,

928
00:41:44,820 --> 00:41:46,580
and what background they've lived through.

929
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:49,000
It's about understanding human nature.

930
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:51,880
You didn't even read the script!

931
00:41:52,350 --> 00:41:53,610
So how did that turn out?

932
00:41:54,760 --> 00:41:56,000
You haven't got a clue!

933
00:42:03,470 --> 00:42:06,600
The reason you nailed
the audition and made it here today

934
00:42:07,730 --> 00:42:09,040
is that that day,

935
00:42:09,510 --> 00:42:11,040
you played as yourself.

936
00:42:11,810 --> 00:42:12,930
Get the picture?

937
00:42:15,210 --> 00:42:17,160
I don't remember it.

938
00:42:17,250 --> 00:42:18,080
Oh, my...

939
00:42:18,590 --> 00:42:19,280
Dead...

940
00:42:19,570 --> 00:42:20,320
We're dead.

941
00:42:21,310 --> 00:42:22,260
Here's what we’ll do, Wan.

942
00:42:22,700 --> 00:42:24,280
Answer my question:

943
00:42:24,810 --> 00:42:26,840
what is Sky,

944
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:29,080
the character you play,

945
00:42:29,710 --> 00:42:30,800
so vengeful about?

946
00:42:32,090 --> 00:42:33,020
Answer me that much.

947
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:41,760
Uh...

948
00:42:42,410 --> 00:42:43,600
I don't know.

949
00:42:44,080 --> 00:42:44,630
I mean...

950
00:42:44,650 --> 00:42:46,310
From what I read in the script earlier,

951
00:42:46,330 --> 00:42:49,140
I don't know why Sky is so vengeful.

952
00:42:49,160 --> 00:42:51,180
Isn't it too nonsensical?

953
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:52,000
Wan!

954
00:42:52,700 --> 00:42:53,700
Have you ever been in a relationship?

955
00:42:53,720 --> 00:42:54,640
Uh, never.

956
00:42:54,660 --> 00:42:55,940
I haven't finished the question.

957
00:42:56,420 --> 00:42:57,260
Listen!

958
00:42:57,640 --> 00:42:58,920
You're not listening!

959
00:42:59,670 --> 00:43:01,160
If your significant other died,

960
00:43:02,050 --> 00:43:03,040
how would you feel?

961
00:43:03,140 --> 00:43:05,080
I've never had one.

962
00:43:05,100 --> 00:43:05,830
But...

963
00:43:05,850 --> 00:43:07,760
I guess I'd be really sad.

964
00:43:07,790 --> 00:43:10,800
But Copter didn't mean to,

965
00:43:10,820 --> 00:43:12,560
so why does he have to be so vindictive?

966
00:43:12,700 --> 00:43:15,140
I'm not Sky, so I can't figure it out.

967
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:15,900
That's the thing!

968
00:43:15,920 --> 00:43:17,640
You don't understand a thing!

969
00:43:17,660 --> 00:43:20,180
No matter what he says,
you never get it!

970
00:43:21,070 --> 00:43:22,300
So what are we gonna do now?

971
00:43:22,780 --> 00:43:23,360
Huh?

972
00:43:23,680 --> 00:43:26,120
Do you suppose
we're ever gonna understand Sky?

973
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:28,040
Uh...

974
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:29,680
I don't know,

975
00:43:29,880 --> 00:43:30,680
but...

976
00:43:30,970 --> 00:43:31,680
Uh...

977
00:43:31,710 --> 00:43:34,320
now that I'm in a workshop,
do I have an acting coach?

978
00:43:42,910 --> 00:43:43,560
Fine.

979
00:43:44,760 --> 00:43:46,200
You want an acting coach?

980
00:43:48,540 --> 00:43:50,020
Then, what do you call these butts

981
00:43:50,240 --> 00:43:51,000
sitting in this room?

982
00:43:51,100 --> 00:43:51,590
Uh...

983
00:43:51,610 --> 00:43:52,800
acting coaches.

984
00:43:54,150 --> 00:43:55,400
Get some sleep, Wan.

985
00:44:01,140 --> 00:44:03,600
For tomorrow's schedule,
you're doing a photo shoot

986
00:44:03,620 --> 00:44:05,780
since there's
a book launch event next Monday.

987
00:44:08,780 --> 00:44:09,440
Hey.

988
00:44:12,510 --> 00:44:13,510
I'm sorry.

989
00:44:13,540 --> 00:44:15,420
I sucked big time today.

990
00:44:23,750 --> 00:44:24,310
Here.

991
00:44:24,330 --> 00:44:25,960
Take a sip to freshen up.

992
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:40,600
This is just the first day,

993
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:43,490
and we did our best.

994
00:44:43,890 --> 00:44:45,680
Who's ever become
a master on their first day?

995
00:44:49,320 --> 00:44:50,400
Let's take a photo,

996
00:44:50,420 --> 00:44:51,600
a Day 1 keepsake.

997
00:45:00,620 --> 00:45:01,240
Wan,

998
00:45:01,940 --> 00:45:03,100
can I take a photo with you, too?

999
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:05,300
Come on.

1000
00:45:10,670 --> 00:45:11,180
Uh...

1001
00:45:11,690 --> 00:45:12,550
Can we do another one?

1002
00:45:12,570 --> 00:45:14,540
It's just that
the lighting falls onto my face.

1003
00:45:14,990 --> 00:45:16,070
Oh, sure.

1004
00:45:16,090 --> 00:45:16,920
Okay.

1005
00:45:23,090 --> 00:45:24,280
Okay, so...

1006
00:45:24,570 --> 00:45:26,120
Post the picture and tag me.

1007
00:45:26,270 --> 00:45:27,880
I wanna share the photo I took with you.

1008
00:45:28,170 --> 00:45:28,810
Sure thing.

1009
00:45:28,830 --> 00:45:29,440
Okay.

1010
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:43,120
[winawann_ mentioned you in their story]

1011
00:45:47,060 --> 00:45:47,820
[nine.nw started following winawann_]

1012
00:45:47,840 --> 00:45:49,640
[nine.nw started following rainjiii]

1013
00:45:53,330 --> 00:45:54,040
Alright.

1014
00:45:55,400 --> 00:45:56,320
So...

1015
00:45:56,690 --> 00:46:00,000
Wan and Renji, you can go home now.

1016
00:46:00,300 --> 00:46:00,930
Alright.

1017
00:46:01,700 --> 00:46:03,000
Nine, you stay.

1018
00:46:03,850 --> 00:46:04,760
Yes, Luang.

1019
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:08,260
Without any bias,

1020
00:46:08,680 --> 00:46:11,680
I don't think Wan is ready
for a series that's about to start filming.

1021
00:46:12,390 --> 00:46:13,400
He seems confused.

1022
00:46:13,840 --> 00:46:14,960
He can't act.

1023
00:46:15,070 --> 00:46:16,880
Above all else,
he doesn't do his homework.

1024
00:46:17,340 --> 00:46:18,900
Um, actually...

1025
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:20,350
I agree with Third.

1026
00:46:20,680 --> 00:46:21,530
True.

1027
00:46:21,780 --> 00:46:23,780
This is pretty damn hard, Pai.

1028
00:46:24,800 --> 00:46:26,560
I'm gonna say this as a director.

1029
00:46:26,900 --> 00:46:29,200
I honestly see some potential in Wan,

1030
00:46:29,690 --> 00:46:30,730
but I've gotta admit.

1031
00:46:30,750 --> 00:46:32,280
It was terrible. He couldn't act at all.

1032
00:46:32,930 --> 00:46:34,140
But I think...

1033
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:35,510
he lacks experience

1034
00:46:35,530 --> 00:46:37,530
and is still finding
his own way in acting.

1035
00:46:37,980 --> 00:46:39,050
Just give him a chance.

1036
00:46:39,070 --> 00:46:39,880
It's only been a day.

1037
00:46:40,310 --> 00:46:41,840
So people who don't
put in effort deserve a chance?

1038
00:46:43,380 --> 00:46:44,470
Third, I have to ask:

1039
00:46:44,740 --> 00:46:46,160
why are you so biased against him?

1040
00:46:46,440 --> 00:46:47,610
This was his first day,

1041
00:46:47,630 --> 00:46:48,880
and he's a rookie.

1042
00:46:49,180 --> 00:46:50,920
Doesn't he need time

1043
00:46:50,940 --> 00:46:51,980
to adjust or something?

1044
00:46:52,000 --> 00:46:54,600
As for all those stupid questions he asked,

1045
00:46:54,620 --> 00:46:56,080
I think that's a good thing.

1046
00:46:56,790 --> 00:46:58,920
It's good to ask questions
when you're clueless,

1047
00:46:59,320 --> 00:47:01,320
and that is
how you put effort into work.

1048
00:47:01,340 --> 00:47:03,720
If you think being unprepared is good,

1049
00:47:04,480 --> 00:47:05,530
then you do you.

1050
00:47:08,470 --> 00:47:09,330
Uh, so...

1051
00:47:09,350 --> 00:47:11,530
Could I voice my opinion?

1052
00:47:12,440 --> 00:47:14,040
I actually think that

1053
00:47:14,060 --> 00:47:15,790
the problem isn't him alone.

1054
00:47:15,810 --> 00:47:17,440
Maybe it's also...

1055
00:47:17,680 --> 00:47:20,140
some other student in the class?

1056
00:47:20,160 --> 00:47:20,840
Well...

1057
00:47:21,850 --> 00:47:23,720
the problem is you're
the only one he's looking at.

1058
00:47:25,280 --> 00:47:27,400
So that'd mean you're also the problem.

1059
00:47:30,830 --> 00:47:31,720
I'm heading out.

1060
00:47:32,270 --> 00:47:33,180
Bye, Luang.

1061
00:47:33,200 --> 00:47:34,280
- Bye, Pai.
- Bye.

1062
00:47:35,170 --> 00:47:36,160
Get home safe.

1063
00:47:39,900 --> 00:47:41,020
I actually...

1064
00:47:41,310 --> 00:47:43,220
don't agree with Third, guys,

1065
00:47:43,240 --> 00:47:44,190
but...

1066
00:47:44,750 --> 00:47:46,930
Wan really can't act.

1067
00:47:47,260 --> 00:47:49,560
It's gonna be a bit hard, isn't it?

1068
00:47:49,820 --> 00:47:50,560
Mm,

1069
00:47:50,780 --> 00:47:51,680
that's right.

1070
00:47:52,200 --> 00:47:55,640
We still have some time
to change our minds, Pai.

1071
00:47:59,440 --> 00:48:00,140
How about this?

1072
00:48:00,520 --> 00:48:02,360
I don't wanna run on dictatorship here.

1073
00:48:02,400 --> 00:48:03,560
Why don't we go ask North?

1074
00:48:04,490 --> 00:48:05,840
Let him settle this.

1075
00:48:08,570 --> 00:48:09,600
Mm...

1076
00:48:11,070 --> 00:48:12,190
Actually...

1077
00:48:12,360 --> 00:48:14,300
it'd be great if we could
quickly talk to North.

1078
00:48:15,170 --> 00:48:15,840
Mm.

1079
00:48:16,890 --> 00:48:18,540
Right, excuse me.

1080
00:48:18,560 --> 00:48:19,730
What's the deal with Renji?

1081
00:48:19,930 --> 00:48:20,920
He was as stiff as a board.

1082
00:48:21,120 --> 00:48:22,200
The acting wasn't good.

1083
00:48:22,220 --> 00:48:23,710
He's the diamond.

1084
00:48:24,910 --> 00:48:27,100
And a diamond
is even stiffer than a board.

1085
00:48:27,120 --> 00:48:27,880
There is...

1086
00:48:27,900 --> 00:48:28,730
shine

1087
00:48:28,750 --> 00:48:29,530
in diamonds.

1088
00:48:29,550 --> 00:48:30,520
Stiffness, sure.

1089
00:48:43,530 --> 00:48:45,520
Do you have a problem
looking at me like that?

1090
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:49,880
I should be the one asking.

1091
00:48:50,610 --> 00:48:52,480
Just tell me you don't like me.

1092
00:48:53,000 --> 00:48:53,720
Sure,

1093
00:48:53,740 --> 00:48:54,740
I don't like you.

1094
00:48:54,760 --> 00:48:55,800
I don't like you, either.

1095
00:48:55,870 --> 00:48:57,100
I'm not asking you to.

1096
00:48:58,100 --> 00:48:59,510
And just so you know,

1097
00:49:00,460 --> 00:49:01,800
you're my coworker now.

1098
00:49:02,320 --> 00:49:04,450
If you suck, then everyone sucks.

1099
00:49:04,470 --> 00:49:05,560
Nine will suck.

1100
00:49:05,730 --> 00:49:07,120
And this series will suck.

1101
00:49:08,250 --> 00:49:10,600
I don't care why you joined the industry,

1102
00:49:12,080 --> 00:49:14,160
but I hate how unprofessional you are.

1103
00:49:22,390 --> 00:49:23,900
And if you keep this up,

1104
00:49:24,800 --> 00:49:26,000
I can remove you from the project.

1105
00:49:26,220 --> 00:49:27,320
What gives you the right?

1106
00:49:27,470 --> 00:49:28,310
I have every right.

1107
00:49:29,400 --> 00:49:30,820
I can even do it right now.

1108
00:49:34,110 --> 00:49:35,680
If you don't value your career,

1109
00:49:36,170 --> 00:49:37,940
at least value your bias's work.

1110
00:49:39,320 --> 00:49:41,160
You wouldn't wanna
ruin his work, would you?

1111
00:49:46,240 --> 00:49:47,650
I don't want to ruin this project.

1112
00:50:14,390 --> 00:50:15,040
Third,

1113
00:50:15,060 --> 00:50:16,560
Pitch is asking for you at the office.

1114
00:50:16,580 --> 00:50:17,620
Both of you.

1115
00:50:17,940 --> 00:50:18,440
Come on.

1116
00:50:30,640 --> 00:50:32,250
How was the workshop?

1117
00:50:34,890 --> 00:50:35,750
It was okay.

1118
00:50:35,770 --> 00:50:36,860
There was no problem.

1119
00:50:38,390 --> 00:50:39,220
Oh...

1120
00:50:40,390 --> 00:50:41,170
except for the new guys.

1121
00:50:41,450 --> 00:50:42,980
Why? What about them?

1122
00:50:43,000 --> 00:50:43,840
Can they not act?

1123
00:50:43,860 --> 00:50:45,260
No, neither one of them can,

1124
00:50:46,010 --> 00:50:47,480
especially the boy named Wan.

1125
00:50:47,780 --> 00:50:48,740
He was late and...

1126
00:50:48,760 --> 00:50:49,900
unprepared.

1127
00:50:51,120 --> 00:50:53,240
Okay, I'll bring this to North's attention

1128
00:50:53,260 --> 00:50:55,480
because it's affecting our team.

1129
00:50:56,980 --> 00:50:58,250
But you two,

1130
00:50:58,270 --> 00:51:00,450
this was the first day of the workshop,

1131
00:51:00,500 --> 00:51:03,320
yet you don't have
a single photo together.

1132
00:51:03,450 --> 00:51:04,630
How was that possible?

1133
00:51:05,090 --> 00:51:06,400
If you don't do it,

1134
00:51:06,810 --> 00:51:08,760
the series will have no buzz.

1135
00:51:08,850 --> 00:51:10,150
And look, the production team said

1136
00:51:10,170 --> 00:51:13,200
you should follow every cast member.

1137
00:51:13,650 --> 00:51:14,390
Uh...

1138
00:51:14,520 --> 00:51:15,650
Nine already did.

